umm, sorry, i won't recant.  i was moved to this after losing a 
20th level valkyrie by walking into a pool and drowning.  to my
dyslexic eye, "{" looks similar enough to "}" ("quick!  which is
the fountain and which is instantly lethal?").  since it left a 
bones level, i tweaked the wizard code, recovered the bones file,
basically recreated the character (wished for a couple scrolls of
identify and remove curse), and then put the game back to normal
mode.

in fact, the character was a tad worse off than the one that
died, since i didn't have maps of the previous levels, and didn't
have knowledge about scrolls/spell books/rings that she had found.

i don't really care much about the scoreboard (i'm the only one
who plays on the system, anyway), so that wasn't really an issue.
i find that being in explore mode (or wizard mode) makes me entirely
to cavalier about my actions--i don't really worry about dying,
so i don't get my reflexes set right (i.e. back away from fights
at the prudent time, etc.).

incidently, i lost another 21 level valkyrie this way (no bones
file, either).  since i've spent entirely too much time playing
nethack at work, i removed the executable (though i'll still play
it here on wet, which is a different system).  while there's a 
certain logic to "{" and "}" for water, i find them entirely
too similar, and too arbitrary a way to die.  perhaps "~" for
all water filled areas?  is there an unused character left?


